---
import { evidenceUrl, url } from "../lib/specs";
---

<section class="recent-progress" aria-labelledby="recent-progress-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Progress · September 23, 2026</p>
  <h2 id="recent-progress-heading">What has changed lately</h2>
  <div class="progress-grid">
    <article>
      <p class="status">Installed and verified</p>
      <h3>Room for apps and updates</h3>
      <p>The system expanded its compact root filesystem on the physical 128 GB
        card, leaving about 119 GB free. A second boot preserved the capacity,
        boot files, shell and Wi-Fi.</p>
      <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/storage-capacity/README.md")}>Storage evidence</a>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="status">Experimental shell · measured on board</p>
      <h3>Finding the card rendering cost</h3>
      <p>A new profile attributes about 98% of repaint CPU to constructing and
        painting frames. After correcting a test setup race, all 13 injected interaction checks
        passed again. Performance targets still fail; a scaled-pixel cache
        comparison is next, and real-finger acceptance remains open.</p>
      <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/card-shell/repaint-stages/README.md")}>Repaint profile and remaining performance gates</a>
      <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/card-shell/throw-fixture-sync/README.md")}>Corrected test and board repeat</a>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="status">Experiment complete</p>
      <h3>CPU vectors tested on the board</h3>
      <p>Vector state and 192 pixel comparisons passed. Card performance gains
        were small and mixed, so the optional vector kernel was not promoted
        to the normal image.</p>
      <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/card-shell/kernel-rvv/card-cost/README.md")}>Measured decision</a>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="next"><strong>Next:</strong> reduce card repaint cost, verify the feel
    with a finger, and refine the shell, launcher, settings and notifications
    into a coherent webOS-inspired interface. That interface is still in development.</p>
  <p class="publication">The requirement count tracks archived specifications.
    This progress summary and the <a href={url("handheld/")}>feature demonstrations</a>
    also report verified work in changes that remain open. Landing a proposal
    does not make it an installed feature.</p>
</section>

<style>
  .recent-progress { max-width: 1080px; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 1.5rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--ink-2); }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); margin: .6rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .progress-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
  article { min-width: 0; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: .5rem 0; }
  p { line-height: 1.65; }
  .status { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .75rem; margin: 0; }
  .next { margin-top: 1.8rem; }
  .publication { font-size: .9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .progress-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
